\f3\fs44 Ministration to the Sick\fs24\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\i\fs20 In case of illness, the Minister of the Congregation is to be notified.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard At the Ministration, one or more parts of the following service are used, as appropriate; but when two or more are used together, they are used in the order indicated.  The Lord's Prayer is always included.\par
\par
Part One of this service may always be led by a deacon or lay person.\par
 \par
When the Laying on of Hands or Anointing takes place at a public celebration of the Eucharist, it is desirable that it precede the distribution of Holy Communion, and it is recommended that it take place immediately before the exchange of the Peace.\par
 \par
The Celebrant begins the service with the following or some other greeting\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Peace be to this house (place), and to all who dwell in it.\par
\pard\sl360\slmult1   \par
\pard\b Part I.  Ministry of the Word\b0\par
 \par
\i\fs20 One or more of the following or other passages of Scripture are read\i0\fs24  \par
 \par
\i General\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 2 Corinthians 1:3-5    (God comforts us in affliction)\par
Psalm 91    (He will give his angels charge over you)\par
Luke 17:11-19    (Your faith has made you well)\fs24\par
\i Penitence\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 Hebrews 12:1-2    (Looking to Jesus, the perfecter of our faith)\par
Psalm 103    (He forgives all your sins)\par
Matthew 9:2-8    (Your sins are forgiven)\fs24\par
 \par
\i When Anointing is to follow\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 James 5:14-16    (Is any among you sick?)\par
Psalm 23    (You have anointed my head with oil)\par
Mark 6:7,12-13    (They anointed with oil many that were sick)\fs24\par
 \par
\i When Communion is to follow\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 1 John 5:13-15    (That you may know that you have eternal life)\par
Psalm 145:14-22    (The eyes of all wait upon you, O Lord)\par
John 6:47-51    (I am the bread of life)\fs24\par
  \par
\i\fs20 After any Reading, the Celebrant may comment on it briefly.\par
 \par
Prayers may be offered according to the occasion.\par
 \par
The Priest may suggest the making of a special confession, if the sick\par
person's conscience is troubled, and use the form for the Reconciliation\par
of a Penitent.\par
 \par
Or else the following general confession may be said\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Most merciful God,\par
we confess that we have sinned against you\par
in thought, word, and deed,\par
by what we have done,\par
and by what we have left undone.\par
We have not loved you with our whole heart;\par
we have not loved our neighbors as ourselves. \par
We are truly sorry and we humbly repent.\par
For the sake of your Son Jesus Christ,\par
have mercy on us and forgive us;\par
that we may delight in your will,\par
and walk in your ways,\par
to the glory of your Name.  Amen.\par
 \par
\i\fs20 The Priest alone says\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God have mercy on you, forgive you all your sins\par
through our Lord Jesus Christ, strengthen you in all goodness,\par
and by the power of the Holy Spirit keep you in eternal life.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\fs20 A deacon or lay person using the preceding form substitutes \ldblquote us\rdblquote  for \ldblquote you\rdblquote  and \ldblquote our\rdblquote  for \ldblquote your.\rdblquote\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b Part II.  Laying on of Hands and Anointing\b0\par
 \par
\i\fs20 If oil for the Anointing of the Sick is to be blessed, the Priest says\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O Lord, holy Father, giver of health and salvation: Send your\par
Holy Spirit to sanctify this oil; that, as your holy apostles\par
anointed many that were sick and healed them, so may those\par
who in faith and repentance receive this holy unction be\par
made whole; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and\par
reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and\par
ever.  \i Amen.\i0\par
  \par
\i\fs20 The following anthem is said\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Savior of the world, by your cross and precious blood you\par
have redeemed us;\par
\i Save us, and help us, we humbly beseech you, O Lord\i0 .\par
  \par
\i\fs20 The Priest then lays hands upon the sick person, and says one of the\par
following\i0\fs24\par
  \par
\par
\i N\i0 ., I lay my hands upon you in the Name of the Father, and\par
of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit, beseeching our Lord Jesus\par
Christ to sustain you with his presence, to drive away all\par
sickness of body and spirit, and to give you that victory of life\par
and peace which will enable you to serve him both now and\par
evermore.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard N.\i0 , I lay my hands upon you in the Name of our Lord and\par
Savior Jesus Christ, beseeching him to uphold you and fill\par
you with his grace, that you may know the healing power of\par
his love.  \i Amen.\par
  \par
\fs20 If the person is to be anointed, the Priest dips a thumb in the holy oil, and makes the sign of the cross on the sick person's forehead, saying\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard N.\i0 , I anoint you with oil in the Name of the Father, and of \par
the Son, and of the Holy Spirit.  \i Amen.\par
  \par
\fs20 The Priest may add\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard As you are outwardly anointed with this holy oil, so may our\par
heavenly Father grant you the inward anointing of the Holy\par
Spirit.  Of his great mercy, may he forgive you your sins,\par
release you from suffering, and restore you to wholeness and\par
strength.  May he deliver you from all evil, preserve you in all\par
goodness, and bring you to everlasting life; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\par
  \par
\fs20 In cases of necessity, a deacon or lay person may perform the\par
anointing, using oil blessed by a bishop or priest.\par
 \par
If Communion is not to follow, the Lord's Prayer is now said.\par
  \par
The Priest concludes\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard The Almighty Lord, who is a strong tower to all who put their\par
trust in him, to whom all things in heaven, on earth, and under\par
the earth bow and obey: Be now and evermore your defense,\par
and make you know and feel that the only Name under\par
heaven given for health and salvation is the Name of our Lord\par
Jesus Christ.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
 \par
\b Part III.  Holy Communion\b0\par
 \par
\i\fs20 If the Eucharist is to be celebrated, the Priest begins with the [Peace\par
and] Offertory.\par
 \par
If Communion is to be administered from the reserved Sacrament, the\par
form for Communion under Special Circumstances is used, beginning with the [Peace and] Lord's Prayer on page 398.\par
 \par
If the sick person cannot receive either the consecrated Bread or the\par
Wine, it is suitable to administer the Sacrament in one kind only.\par
 \par
One of the usual postcommunion prayers is said, or the following\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Gracious Father, we give you praise and thanks for this Holy\par
Communion of the Body and Blood of your beloved Son\par
Jesus Christ, the pledge of our redemption; and we pray that\par
it may bring us forgiveness of our sins, strength in our\par
weakness, and everlasting salvation; through Jesus Christ\par
our Lord.  \i Amen.\par
  \par
\fs20 The service concludes with a blessing or with a dismissal\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \i0\par
\pard Let us bless the Lord.\par
\i Thanks be to God.\par
 \par
\fs20 If a person desires to receive the Sacrament, but, by reason of extreme\par
sickness or physical disability, is unable to eat and drink the Bread\par
and Wine, the Celebrant is to assure that person that all the benefits\par
of Communion are received, even though the Sacrament is not received\par
with the mouth.\i0\fs24\par
\b\par
Prayers for the Sick\b0\par
  \par
\i For a Sick Person\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O Father of mercies and God of all comfort, our only help in\par
time of need: We humbly beseech thee to behold, visit, and\par
relieve thy sick servant \i N.\i0  for whom our prayers are desired.\par
Look upon \i him\i0  with the eyes of thy mercy; comfort \i him\i0  with\par
a sense of thy goodness; preserve \i him\i0  from the temptations\par
of the enemy; and give \i him\i0  patience under \i his\i0  affliction. In\par
thy good time, restore \i him\i0  to health, and enable \i him\i0  to lead\par
the residue of \i his\i0  life in thy fear, and to thy glory; and grant\par
that finally \i he\i0  may dwell with thee in life everlasting; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i For Recovery from Sickness\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, the strength of the weak and the comfort of sufferers:\par
Mercifully accept our prayers, and grant to your servant \i N\i0 .\par
the help of your power, that \i his\i0  sickness may be turned into\par
health, and our sorrow into joy; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God of heavenly powers, by the might of your command\par
you drive away from our bodies all sickness and all infirmity:\par
Be present in your goodness with your servant \i N\i0 ., that \i his\i0\par
weakness may be banished and his strength restored; and that,\par
his health being renewed, \i he\i0  may bless your holy Name;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\par
 \par
For a Sick Child\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Heavenly Father, watch with us over your child \i N\i0 ., and grant\par
that \i he\i0  may be restored to that perfect health which it is\par
yours alone to give; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\i\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Lord Jesus Christ, Good Shepherd of the sheep, you gather\par
the lambs in your arms and carry them in your bosom: We\par
commend to your loving care this child \i N\i0 .  Relieve \i his\i0  pain,\par
guard \i him\i0  from all danger, restore to \i him\i0  your gifts of\par
gladness and strength, and raise \i him\i0  up to a life of service to\par
you.  Hear us, we pray, for your dear Name's sake. \i Amen. \par
 \par
Before an Operation\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God our heavenly Father, graciously comfort your\par
servant \i N\i0 . in \i his\i0  suffering, and bless the means made use of\par
for \i his\i0  cure. Fill \i his\i0  heart with confidence that, though at times \i he\i0  may be afraid, he yet may put \i his\i0  trust in you; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Strengthen your servant \i N\i0 ., O God, to do what \i he\i0  has to do\par
and bear what \i he\i0  has to bear; that, accepting your healing\par
gifts through the skill of surgeons and nurses, \i he\i0  may be\par
restored to usefulness in your world with a thankful heart; through Jesus Christ our Lord. \i Amen\i0 . \par
 \par
\i For Strength and Confidence\i0\par
 \par
Heavenly Father, giver of life and health: Comfort and\par
relieve your sick servant \i N\i0 ., and give your power of healing to\par
those who minister to \i his\i0  needs, that \i he\i0  may be strengthened in \i his\i0  weakness and have confidence in your loving care; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\par
\i For the Sanctification of Illness\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Sanctify, O Lord, the sickness of your servant \i N\i0 ., that the\par
sense of \i his\i0  weakness may add strength to \i his\i0  faith and\par
seriousness to \i his\i0  repentance; and grant that \i he\i0  may live with\par
you in everlasting life; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  \i Amen.\i0  \par
 \par
\i For Health of Body and Soul\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard May God the Father bless you, God the Son heal you, God\par
the Holy Spirit give you strength.  May God the holy and\par
undivided Trinity guard your body, save your soul, and bring\par
you safely to his heavenly country; where he lives and reigns\par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen. \par
 \par
For Doctors and Nurses\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Sanctify, O Lord, those whom you have called to the study\par
and practice of the arts of healing, and to the prevention of\par
disease and pain. Strengthen them by your life-giving Spirit,\par
that by their ministries the health of the community may be\par
promoted and your creation glorified; through Jesus Christ\par
our Lord.  \i Amen. \par
 \par
Thanksgiving for a Beginning of Recovery\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O Lord, your compassions never fail and your mercies are\par
new every morning: We give you thanks for giving our\par
brother (sister) \i N\i0 . both relief from pain and hope of health\par
renewed.  Continue in \i him\i0 , we pray, the good work you have\par
begun; that \i he\i0 , daily increasing in bodily strength, and\par
rejoicing in your goodness, may so order \i his\i0  life and conduct\par
that \i he\i0  may always think and do those things that please\par
you; through Jesus Christ our Lord. \i Amen\i0 .\par
\par
\b Prayers for use by a Sick Person\b0\par
\par
\i For Trust in God\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard O God, the source of all health: So fill my heart with faith in\par
your love, that with calm expectancy I may make room for\par
your power to possess me, and gracefully accept your\par
healing; through Jesus Christ our Lord.  Amen. \i\par
 \par
In Pain\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Lord Jesus Christ, by your patience in suffering you hallowed\par
earthly pain and gave us the example of obedience to your\par
Father's will: Be near me in my time of weakness and pain;\par
sustain me by your grace, that my strength and courage may\par
not fail; heal me according to your will; and help me always\par
to believe that what happens to me here is of little account if\par
you hold me in eternal life, my Lord and my God. Amen. \par
 \par
\i For Sleep\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O heavenly Father, you give your children sleep for the\par
refreshing of soul and body: Grant me this gift, I pray; keep\par
me in that perfect peace which you have promised to those\par
whose minds are fixed on you; and give me such a sense of\par
your presence, that in the hours of silence I may enjoy the\par
blessed assurance of your love; through Jesus Christ our\par
Savior.  Amen. \i\par
 \par
In the Morning\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard This is another day, O Lord.  I know not what it will bring\par
forth, but make me ready, Lord, for whatever it may be.  If I\par
am to stand up, help me to stand bravely. If I am to sit still,\par
help me to sit quietly. If I am to lie low, help me to do it\par
patiently.  And if I am to do nothing, let me do it gallantly.\par
Make these words more than words, and give me the Spirit\par
of Jesus.  Amen.\par
}
